  "description": "Neon Ooze is an aesthetic that developed in the 80s and 90s and was used most commonly for targeting children through gross-out marketing. The driving visual element were fluids such as slime, goop or toxic waste, with other related elements often thrown in such as nuclear, mad science or \"creepy crawly\" imagery. It reflects an era's playful obsession with eco-anxiety and gross-out humor.",
